{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Run an LDAP directory on node1 for dc=branch,dc=test and import the staged LDIF without altering the supplied user identities or mail addresses.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The staged LDIF defines alex/Alex North/alex@branch.test and sam/Sam West/sam@branch.test. Final direct searches show those same entries and attributes under ou=people,dc=branch,dc=test; node1's directory service is active, enabled, and listening on port 389 after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-0f62309194a54c37","cmd-6c3a983242714eb9","cmd-27ba21fe5bf647a4","cmd-9bd2591a89f54a98"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Allow node2 to search the people subtree and find both imported users.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Anonymous remote searches from node2 directly returned both alex and sam with the expected names and mail addresses, both before and after the node restarts.","evidence_ids":["cmd-0d4dac6a1b9647b1","cmd-df582093545c46ec","cmd-1bede3cf1da048e9","cmd-142dd56cc6144a86"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Require authenticated administration for directory updates and reject anonymous writes.","status":"satisfied","summary":"A Directory Manager bind successfully added a test attribute, verified it, and removed it. Anonymous modification attempts from node2 failed with LDAP error 50, and subsequent searches confirmed that neither attempted value persisted, including after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-b9129724361348d3","cmd-95ac9e9dcdff4a65","cmd-142dd56cc6144a86"]},{"id":"R4","requirement":"Retain the installed operating-system release and kernel while using software compatible with the legacy platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Both nodes remained on RHEL 10.0 with kernel 6.12.0-55.9.1.el10_0.x86_64. The directory server and LDAP clients were installed from the configured RHEL 10 repositories, and package-health observations remained clean.","evidence_ids":["cmd-5025c0202e6e4e63","cmd-5d6d6dd65b6343bd","cmd-87aebda352804074","cmd-36ebe0e5ced44d73","cmd-9bd2591a89f54a98","cmd-142dd56cc6144a86","global:after_executor:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node2:platform","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:package-health"]}],"confidence":0.98,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.99,"summary":"No clearly established unnecessary mutation or unwanted residue was found. Package installation, directory creation, persistent firewall access, data import, bounded access-control tests, and required restarts all had direct roles in the requested outcome or its verification. The authenticated test update was fully reverted. Failed add attempts show no unsupported data mutation. One troubleshooting command may have reset the administrator password to the already intended value, but its output does not establish whether a mutation occurred or contributed; it is therefore treated as an evidence limitation rather than a proven hygiene violation. Final snapshots show no failed services or damaged package state, and the added port 389 listener is required by the task.","evidence_ids":["cmd-d16fe384b93a449c","cmd-b9129724361348d3","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node2:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct final-state and behavioral evidence. The provider-wide restart protocol was also completed coherently on both nodes: each has a healthy pre-restart observation, restart acknowledgement, changed boot identity, and recovered relevant service/client and directory data. Fixed lifecycle boot identities independently corroborate both restarts.","limitations":["The trace does not establish whether cmd-d16fe384b93a449c actually changed the administrator password; subsequent evidence only shows that the intended credential worked.","The staged LDIF file itself was not re-hashed after execution, although the imported final attributes directly match its captured contents.","Node2 hosts only the LDAP client, so its post-restart recovery evidence appropriately demonstrates client-package presence and successful remote directory access rather than a local LDAP service."]}
